    "summary": {
      "plain": "The Spallation Neutron Source at Oak Ridge National Laboratory, Tennessee, shown here as its outer accelerator/target complex boundary: the linac, accumulator ring and the COHERENT experiment's Neutrino Alley all lie somewhere within this footprint, but none has its own separately-sourced path or position this session."
    },
    "type": "map",
    "unlocated": [
      {
        "backlog": "A candidate for the linac building was found and deliberately NOT drawn: unlabeled OpenStreetMap way 892578460 inside the SNS complex is an unusually long, thin rectangle (measured span 370 m, area 5,294 sq m, implied width approx 14 m) geometrically consistent with the published linac-length range, but it carries no name or other identifying tag, so identifying it as the linac would be this researcher's inference, not a sourced claim. A future pass should confirm it (or find the actual linac/ring building) via an official annotated aerial photo, a civil-engineering site plan, or by retrying a fuller Overpass query (name/landuse tags, the accumulator ring's characteristic near-circular shape) once a mirror answers reliably within its timeout.",
        "entity_id": "accelerator:sns",
        "entity_name": "Spallation Neutron Source",
        "entity_type": "accelerator",
        "reason": "The SNS's ~305-330 m linac (sources disagree across eras: '1,000-foot linac' [305 m] per src:geo-ornl-sns-cold-linac-2005, a 2005 pre-completion article; other official pages describe a '355-yard' [~325 m] linac; a 493 m post-Proton-Power-Upgrade total appears only in unfetched secondary summaries and is not used here) and its 271-yard (~248 m) accumulator ring (src:geo-ornl-sns-ppu-ring) are both inside the complex boundary drawn as geometry:sns-complex-boundary. A later Overpass mirror (maps.mail.ru) did return the complex's 25 individual building footprints, none named or tagged beyond generic 'building=yes'/'service' (one unrelated 'ORNL Guest House'), so no building can be honestly identified as the linac or ring without guessing from shape alone; see the backlog for the one shape-only candidate found.",
        "sources": [
          "src:geo-ornl-sns-cold-linac-2005",
          "src:geo-ornl-sns-ppu-ring"
        ]
      }
    ]
